event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":125,"item_id":"rs_0b031b0068ea2d96016ac956d9b3488196887f25d53f407e11","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing SSR Forms**\n\nI need to set up simple server-side rendered (SSR) forms with HTTP routes that work in the browser without requiring JavaScript, using just HTML. When a POST form is submitted, it should redirect on invalid input and render a 400 alert while keeping a list. I'll also need to encode the responses properly. Testing involves using Node's built-in spawn for a temporary test database, restarting for health checks on POST requests. The API isn't necessary here, and the project route should handle resource max body limits, using inline static CSS to keep it simple. I should remember to add a test script as well."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":126,"item_id":"rs_0b031b0068ea2d96016ac956d9b3488196887f25d53f407e11","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing SSR Forms**\n\nI need to set up simple server-side rendered (SSR) forms with HTTP routes that work in the browser without requiring JavaScript, using just HTML. When a POST form is submitted, it should redirect on invalid input and render a 400 alert while keeping a list. I'll also need to encode the responses properly. Testing involves using Node's built-in spawn for a temporary test database, restarting for health checks on POST requests. The API isn't necessary here, and the project route should handle resource max body limits, using inline static CSS to keep it simple. I should remember to add a test script as well."}}

